  "extraction_notes": [
    "Source: All Power Semiconductor AP5N10S SOT-23-3L N-channel 100 V MOSFET datasheet, revision v1.0, 6 pages; SHA-256 of the PDF verified against the briefed value before extraction.",
    "All numeric quantities are SI: resistances in ohms (115 mOhm -> 0.115), capacitances in farads (210 pF -> 2.1e-10 F) for both specs and the Figure 9 curve y-axes; currents in amperes (250 uA -> 2.5e-4 A).",
    "Curves were digitized visually from raster figures: Figure 6 (transfer, V_DS = 10 V, T_J = 25 C, log I_D axis), Figure 3 (output characteristics, one series per V_GS from 3.5 V to 10 V), and Figure 9 (Ciss/Coss/Crss vs V_DS at f = 100 kHz, V_GS = 0 V, log pF axis converted to F).",
    "Transfer-curve points were cross-checked against Figure 3 saturation plateaus (V_GS = 4 V -> ~4 A, 5 V -> ~10.5 A, 10 V -> ~17 A) and are mutually consistent; capacitance curves were anchored to the page 2 table values at V_DS = 25 V (Ciss 210 pF, Coss 30 pF, Crss 14 pF; table measured at 1 MHz, figure at 100 kHz).",
    "Digitized points carry graph-reading uncertainty of roughly 5-10 percent, larger on the log-axis capacitance tails; table-sourced specs are exact transcriptions.",
    "Datasheet header brand is ALLPOWER / All Power Semiconductor co.,Ltd; target manufacturer identity preserved as briefed.",
    "Additional figures present but not digitized: Fig 1-2 deratings, Fig 4/7 Rdson vs I_D and vs T_J, Fig 5 BVdss vs T_J, Fig 8 gate charge, Fig 10 SOA, Fig 11 body-diode forward. No vendor SPICE model content was used; public datasheet evidence only."
